      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.2,
          "end": 3.92,
          "en": "The source folder contains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.92,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "all the JavaScript files we're going to write code in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 11.58,
          "en": "In the end, the source folder is our main working directory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.58,
          "end": 14.35,
          "en": "We're going to write our Vue application code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.35,
          "end": 15.843,
          "en": "in that source folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.84,
          "end": 20.8,
          "en": "The main JavaScript file here is the main entry point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.8,
          "end": 24.06,
          "en": "And here you see we've got an import syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.06,
          "end": 26.02,
          "en": "which we haven't used thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.02,
          "end": 28.93,
          "en": "but that is actually default JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.93,
          "end": 32.69,
          "en": "a modern JavaScript feature for importing functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.69,
          "end": 35.25,
          "en": "from one file into another file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.25,
          "end": 38.5,
          "en": "And here we're importing the createApp function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.5,
          "end": 40.94,
          "en": "from the Vue framework.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.94,
          "end": 42.653,
          "en": "Before we used vue.createApp,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.806,
          "end": 46.36,
          "en": "now we don't do that because now we don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.36,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "a globally available Vue object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 52.04,
          "en": "but instead we can now import from the Vue framework",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.04,
          "end": 56.03,
          "en": "and import things like the createApp method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.03,
          "end": 60.19,
          "en": "And then we create an app with a configuration that seems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.19,
          "end": 63.99,
          "en": "to come from the App.vue file, more on that in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.99,
          "end": 68.2,
          "en": "and we mount it to an element with an ID of app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.2,
          "end": 71.83,
          "en": "And that's just this div here with the ID app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.83,
          "end": 74.17,
          "en": "in that index HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.17,
          "end": 76.82300000000001,
          "en": "So that's how our Vue app ends up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 80.89,
          "en": "So it's a different way of calling createApp",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.89,
          "end": 83.27,
          "en": "by using this import syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.27,
          "end": 85.44,
          "en": "but we're going to use this import syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.44,
          "end": 86.99,
          "en": "throughout this course from now on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.99,
          "end": 90.96000000000001,
          "en": "because this is the modern JavaScript way of exporting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.96000000000001,
          "end": 93.893,
          "en": "and importing features from one file to another.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.12,
          "end": 97.81,
          "en": "But what about this App.vue file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.81,
          "end": 101.09,
          "en": "I mean, createApp always took this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.09,
          "end": 102.8,
          "en": "with the data and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.8,
          "end": 105.44,
          "en": "So why are we now passing app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.44,
          "end": 109.82,
          "en": "which is coming from the App.vue file to createApp?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.82,
          "end": 112.08,
          "en": "Well, let's see what's in App.vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.527,
          "end": 117.47,
          "en": ".vue files are a special Vue.JS feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.47,
          "end": 122.47,
          "en": "or a special Vue CLI project feature, I could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.847,
          "end": 128.847,
          "en": ".vue file allow us to right Vue apps and to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.22,
          "end": 133.73,
          "en": "Vue components specifically in a much nicer way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.73,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "They allow us to split our template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 141.57999999999998,
          "en": "so the HTML code that belongs to an app or a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.57999999999998,
          "end": 144.61,
          "en": "the script part and also some styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.61,
          "end": 148.31,
          "en": "into three different sections here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.31,
          "end": 153.03,
          "en": "You see, we have a template tag here in this Vue file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.03,
          "end": 155.63,
          "en": "which contains the template of this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.63,
          "end": 159.22,
          "en": "a script tag, which contains actually this conflict object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.22,
          "end": 162.41,
          "en": "we saw before, just with different keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.41,
          "end": 164.25,
          "en": "which we haven't seen before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 168.23,
          "en": "but this indeed is where you also would add your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.23,
          "end": 171.89,
          "en": "But we'll have a look at that in greater detail in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.89,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "And we have a style tag here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 179.09,
          "en": "which allows us to define the styles, the CSS styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.09,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "that should be available in this Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 186.04,
          "en": "And this is a file which would not work like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.04,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "in the browser, but which Vue CLI will transform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 193.19,
          "en": "behind the scenes to a code that will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.19,
          "end": 196.54,
          "en": "So that, we as a developer, have a nice way of defining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.54,
          "end": 199.5,
          "en": "our Vue apps with three sections like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.5,
          "end": 201.8,
          "en": "and we still will end up with code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.8,
          "end": 204.52,
          "en": "that just works in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.52,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "But how exactly does this work and why might we want this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.55,
          "end": 213.5,
          "en": "In the end, the project, which we created with the Vue CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.5,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "uses a so-called build workflow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 219.85,
          "en": "That's a fancy way of saying that the code we write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.85,
          "end": 222.67000000000002,
          "en": "is not the code that runs in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.67000000000002,
          "end": 226.98,
          "en": "Instead, our code has certain features, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 229.38,
          "en": "next-gen JavaScript features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 232.32,
          "en": "but also Vue specific features and syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.32,
          "end": 234.32999999999998,
          "en": "like the .vue files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 237.09300000000002,
          "en": "which wouldn't work like that in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.07,
          "end": 241.16,
          "en": "If you try to load a .vue file with the structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.16,
          "end": 244.91,
          "en": "you just saw in the browser, it simply wouldn't do anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.91,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "because the browser doesn't know what to do with that code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 250.51,
          "en": "But that's the important thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.51,
          "end": 255.15,
          "en": "Now, the project generated with the Vue CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.15,
          "end": 260.15,
          "en": "has a lot of under the hood tools working on our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 260.92,
          "end": 265.5,
          "en": "to transform that code in a so-called built step to code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 265.5,
          "end": 267.11,
          "en": "that works in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.11,
          "end": 269.12,
          "en": "So that build step is simply just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 269.12,
          "end": 272.56,
          "en": "a couple of transformations being applied to our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.56,
          "end": 276.15999999999997,
          "en": "to change that code to standard JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 276.15999999999997,
          "end": 278.74,
          "en": "with standard JavaScript features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 278.74,
          "end": 281.12,
          "en": "that do work in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.12,
          "end": 284.21,
          "en": "And then the development or a real web server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 284.21,
          "end": 288.15999999999997,
          "en": "that hosts our app is able to show something on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 288.15999999999997,
          "end": 291.34000000000003,
          "en": "because it only receives regular JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 291.34000000000003,
          "end": 293.75,
          "en": "that just works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 293.75,
          "end": 296.73,
          "en": "And at the end, our project also has such a setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 296.73,
          "end": 298.35,
          "en": "under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.35,
          "end": 300.49,
          "en": "In the end, the npm run service script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 300.49,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "does not just spin up that development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 305.72,
          "en": "but also start this build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.72,
          "end": 308.95,
          "en": "which watches our code files and transforms to code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.95,
          "end": 311.2,
          "en": "And that's my code like this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.2,
          "end": 314.11,
          "en": "with a separate template, script, and style tech,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.11,
          "end": 317.28,
          "en": "in the end is transformed to just JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 317.28,
          "end": 319.233,
          "en": "which runs in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 320.63,
          "end": 323.59,
          "en": "And this is a good thing because you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 323.59,
          "end": 327.554,
          "en": "throughout the course that those .vue files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 327.554,
          "end": 330.48,
          "en": "are also called signal file components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 330.48,
          "end": 333.06,
          "en": "that those single file components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.06,
          "end": 337.43,
          "en": "are a pretty convenient way of writing Vue components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.43,
          "end": 340,
          "en": "and writing Vue code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340,
          "end": 341.35,
          "en": "On the other end at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 341.35,
